> Go for it.

Be careful.  The Samurai quest nemisis has the Tsurugi of
Muramasa, and will pick it up and use it.  With a 5% chance of
instantly killing you with each hit.  I'd recommend some means
of instakill before taking him on.  (Alternatively, you should
be able to put him to sleep, and kill him when he's sleeping.)

    [...]
> > weapon skills:
> > twoweapon: unskilled
> > long sword: expert
> > saber: basic
> > bow: skilled
> > spells: attack and clerical unskilled

> Probably not worth enhancing spells until you have XP slots to
> spare.  You will get a huge gain from bow to expert and
> a smaller but large gain from moving twoweapon up.

Samurai can two weapon effectively.  Grayswandir and a silver
saber will wreck havoc in Gehemmon, and either Grayswandir or
Excalibur with a katana elsewhere.  (Grayswandir and a sliver
saber, along with the two hits you get because of your speed,
will often kill a named demon before he has a chance to teleport
to the stairs up.)

I'd increase bow to expert, and twoweapon to skilled, before I'd
start thinking about spells.

